 # @acme/ui
 
-Accessible React components.
+Accessible React components: Tabs, Dialog and Combobox. Each follows its WAI-ARIA Authoring
+Practices pattern, takes no CSS, and passes extra props (including `className`) to its main element.
+
+Run `pnpm test` for the tests and `pnpm typecheck` for the type check.
+
+```tsx
+import { Combobox, Dialog, Tab, TabList, TabPanel, Tabs } from "@acme/ui";
+
+<Tabs defaultValue="profile">
+  <TabList aria-label="Settings">
+    <Tab value="profile">Profile</Tab>
+    <Tab value="billing">Billing</Tab>
+  </TabList>
+  <TabPanel value="profile">Profile form</TabPanel>
+  <TabPanel value="billing">Billing form</TabPanel>
+</Tabs>;
+
+<Dialog open={open} onOpenChange={setOpen} title="Delete project" description="This cannot be undone.">
+  <button type="button" onClick={() => setOpen(false)}>Cancel</button>
+</Dialog>;
+
+<Combobox
+  label="Fruit"
+  options={[{ value: "apple", label: "Apple" }, { value: "pear", label: "Pear", disabled: true }]}
+  value={fruit}
+  onChange={setFruit}
+  placeholder="Search fruit"
+/>;
+```
+
+## Tabs
+
+Automatic activation: moving focus with the arrow keys selects the tab. Tab order and
+wrap-around come from the DOM order of the tabs. The selection is the `value` prop when given
+(controlled), otherwise internal state seeded by `defaultValue` (uncontrolled). If the selected
+value is missing or disabled, the first enabled tab is selected. Re-selecting the selected tab
+does not call `onValueChange`.
+
+| Name | Type | Default | Description |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| `value` | `string` (Tabs) | — | Controlled selected value. The parent must update it in `onValueChange`. |
+| `defaultValue` | `string` (Tabs) | first enabled tab | Initial value when uncontrolled. |
+| `onValueChange` | `(value: string) => void` (Tabs) | — | Called when the user selects a tab, in both modes. |
+| `aria-label` | `string` (TabList) | required | Accessible name for the tablist. |
+| `value` | `string` (Tab, TabPanel) | required | Identifies the tab and its panel. |
+| `disabled` | `boolean` (Tab) | `false` | Disables the tab: it cannot be clicked or focused by the arrow keys. |
+| `className` | `string` | — | Applied to the Tabs wrapper, TabList, Tab, or TabPanel element. |
+
+Using `Tab`, `TabList` or `TabPanel` outside `<Tabs>` throws.
+
+| Key | Action |
+| --- | --- |
+| `ArrowRight` / `ArrowLeft` | Next / previous enabled tab, wrapping at both ends. Selects it. |
+| `Home` / `End` | First / last enabled tab. Selects it. |
+| `Tab` | Moves from the tablist to the selected panel. |
+
+## Dialog
+
+Modal dialog rendered into `document.body` through a portal, with a backdrop. Focus moves to
+the first focusable element on open (or to the dialog itself if there is none) and returns to
+the previously focused element on close. Tab and Shift+Tab are trapped inside. Disabled
+controls, `tabindex="-1"` elements, and elements that are not rendered are skipped. An element is
+not rendered when it or an ancestor up to the dialog has the `hidden` attribute, is `inert`, or has
+`display: none`, or when its own computed `visibility` is `hidden`. Visibility is inherited, so a
+child with `visibility: visible` under a hidden parent is still focusable. The dialog never
+closes itself; it only calls `onOpenChange(false)`. Body scroll is not locked.
+
+| Name | Type | Default | Description |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| `open` | `boolean` | required | Whether the dialog is shown. Nothing is rendered when `false`. |
+| `onOpenChange` | `(open: boolean) => void` | required | Called with `false` on Escape or a backdrop click. |
+| `title` | `ReactNode` | required | Rendered as an `h2` and used as the accessible name. |
+| `description` | `ReactNode` | — | Rendered as a paragraph and referenced by `aria-describedby`. Omitted when `undefined`, `null` or `false`. |
+| `className` | `string` | — | Applied to the dialog element. |
+
+| Key | Action |
+| --- | --- |
+| `Escape` | Calls `onOpenChange(false)`. |
+| `Tab` / `Shift+Tab` | Moves focus forward / backward, wrapping inside the dialog. |
+
+A click on the backdrop calls `onOpenChange(false)`. A click inside the dialog, or a drag that
+starts inside and ends on the backdrop, does not.
+
+## Combobox
+
+Text input with a listbox popup (list autocomplete). Typing or clicking the input opens the
+listbox and filters options by a case-insensitive substring match on the label. The input shows
+the selected option's label when not editing. Choosing an option calls `onChange(value)`.
+Clearing the text does not call `onChange(null)`: leaving the input or pressing Escape restores
+the selected label. A `value` that matches no option shows an empty input. When the parent
+changes `value`, any typed text is discarded and the input shows the new option's label.
+
+When nothing matches, a "No results" message is shown beside the listbox rather than inside it.
+An active option that is removed from the visible list is cleared, so Enter does not choose it.
+
+Arrow navigation wraps at both ends and skips disabled options. Escape while the listbox is open
+closes it and stops the event from reaching an enclosing Dialog. Escape while it is closed is not
+handled, so an enclosing Dialog can close.
+
+| Name | Type | Default | Description |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| `label` | `string` | required | Visible label, associated with the input. Also names the listbox. |
+| `options` | `ComboboxOption[]` | required | Options with `value`, `label` and optional `disabled`. |
+| `value` | `string \| null` | required | Selected option value, or `null` for no selection. |
+| `onChange` | `(value: string \| null) => void` | required | Called when the user chooses an enabled option. Never called for clearing. |
+| `placeholder` | `string` | — | Forwarded to the input. |
+| `className` | `string` | — | Applied to the input. |
+
+| Key | Action |
+| --- | --- |
+| `ArrowDown` | Opens the listbox if closed; otherwise moves the active option forward (wrapping). |
+| `ArrowUp` | Moves the active option backward (wrapping) while open. |
+| `Enter` | While open: chooses the active enabled option, if any, and never submits the form. While closed: native behaviour. |
+| `Escape` | While open: closes without calling `onChange` and restores the selected label. |
+
+Focus stays in the input. The active option is exposed through `aria-activedescendant`, and a
+`data-active` attribute is set on it for styling. Clicking an enabled option chooses it. Leaving
+the input closes the listbox and restores the selected label without calling `onChange`.
